  "units": [
    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealComplexOperator.exists_positive_complex_lift",
      "title": "Positive real L² operator: actual complexification",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A4",
          "label": "Appendix D.1 real Hilbert conventions and positive square-root background; B.10-B.11 actual all-macro square-root prerequisite, attributed ASTIS complexification completion, not a printed paper theorem.",
          "scope": "No root, real descent of complex CFC root, uniqueness, Gamma0/B15/B16, weakH1/dynamics/main/error/querycost/composition, paper or Goal closure."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.ProximalBPSDefectComplexLift"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Let Ω be an arbitrary measurable space, μ any measure, and D a bounded positive real-linear endomorphism of L²(μ;ℝ). Positivity includes selfadjointness. Define the actual quotient maps ιu=u+0i, Rg=Re g, Qg=Im g and Cg=conj(g) via Mathlib compLpL.",
        "No finite/probability measure, finite-dimensional L2, nontriviality, chosen embedding or CFC input.",
        "Pointwise conjugation C is real linear; it is distinct from operator adjoint. Complex-root preservation and descent remain separate obligations."
      ],
      "statement": "Let Ω be an arbitrary measurable space, μ any measure, and D a bounded positive real-linear endomorphism of L²(μ;ℝ). Positivity includes selfadjointness. Define the actual quotient maps ιu=u+0i, Rg=Re g, Qg=Im g and Cg=conj(g) via Mathlib compLpL. The embedding preserves norm: ‖ιu‖=‖u‖ for every u, and its full range is exactly the fixed space of C: Cg=g iff there exists u with ιu=g. There exists a bounded complex-linear positive operator Dc on L²(μ;ℂ), with for every g, Dc g=ιD(Rg)+iιD(Qg), for every real u, Dc(ιu)=ι(Du), and for every complex g, C(Dc g)=Dc(Cg). No root or inverse is asserted.",
      "formula": "\\operatorname{Fix}(C)=\\operatorname{ran}(\\iota),\\quad D_{\\mathbb C}(\\iota a+i\\iota b)=\\iota Da+i\\iota Db,\\quad D_{\\mathbb C}\\ge0,\\quad D_{\\mathbb C}\\iota=\\iota D,\\quad CD_{\\mathbb C}=D_{\\mathbb C}C.",
      "boundary": "No root, real descent of complex CFC root, uniqueness, Gamma0/B15/B16, weakH1/dynamics/main/error/querycost/composition, paper or Goal closure.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Construct the actual quotient maps",
          "text": "The scalar maps ofReal, Re, Im and conjugation are bounded real-linear maps. compLpL carries them to the same AE quotient spaces. Its AE representative formula proves Rι=I, Qι=0 and ιRg+iιQg=g. No representative is chosen as an additional input.",
          "formula": "R\\iota u=u,\\quad Q\\iota u=0,\\quad g=\\iota Rg+i\\iota Qg.",
          "lean": "real_embed; imag_embed; parts"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the real subspace and its norm",
          "text": "Integrating the pointwise inner products gives ⟨ιu,ιv⟩ℂ=⟨u,v⟩ℝ. Thus ι preserves norm. The equality Cg=g implies Im g=0 almost everywhere, so g=ιRg; the converse follows from conjugating a real value. This proves the exact fixed range for arbitrary μ.",
          "formula": "\\langle\\iota u,\\iota v\\rangle_{\\mathbb C}=\\langle u,v\\rangle_{\\mathbb R},\\quad\\|\\iota u\\|=\\|u\\|,\\quad\\operatorname{Fix}(C)=\\operatorname{ran}(\\iota).",
          "lean": "inner_embed; norm_embed; conjugate_embed; fixed_range"
        },
        {
          "title": "Build a bounded complex-linear operator",
          "text": "First form the bounded real-linear map Dc g=ιD(Rg)+iιD(Qg). The identities R(ig)=−Qg and Q(ig)=Rg show Dc(ig)=iDc g. Writing c=Re c+i Im c upgrades real linearity to complex linearity, while preserving the already proved continuity.",
          "formula": "D_{\\mathbb C}g=\\iota D(Rg)+i\\iota D(Qg),\\quad D_{\\mathbb C}(cg)=cD_{\\mathbb C}g.",
          "lean": "real_I; imag_I; liftReal; liftReal_I; liftComplex"
        },
        {
          "title": "Cancel the imaginary cross terms",
          "text": "Expand the complex inner product at g=ιa+iιb, where a=Rg,b=Qg. Real selfadjointness gives ⟨Db,a⟩ℝ=⟨Da,b⟩ℝ, cancelling the imaginary cross terms. The remaining two real quadratic forms are nonnegative by the original positivity of D.",
          "formula": "\\langle D_{\\mathbb C}g,g\\rangle_{\\mathbb C}=\\langle Da,a\\rangle_{\\mathbb R}+\\langle Db,b\\rangle_{\\mathbb R}\\ge0.",
          "lean": "inner_lift; liftComplex_positive; ContinuousLinearMap.isPositive_iff_complex"
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove both compatibility identities",
          "text": "On real inputs, Rι=I and Qι=0 give Dcι=ιD. Conjugation preserves the real part and negates the imaginary part; substituting into the literal formula gives CDc=DcC. Operator adjoint and pointwise conjugation are distinct operations.",
          "formula": "D_{\\mathbb C}\\iota=\\iota D,\\quad CD_{\\mathbb C}=D_{\\mathbb C}C.",
          "lean": "liftComplex_embed; real_conjugate; imag_conjugate; liftComplex_conjugate"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let Ω be an arbitrary measurable space, μ any measure, and D a bounded positive real-linear endomorphism of L²(μ;ℝ). Positivity includes selfadjointness. Define the actual quotient maps ιu=u+0i, Rg=Re g, Qg=Im g and Cg=conj(g) via Mathlib compLpL. The embedding preserves norm: ‖ιu‖=‖u‖ for every u, and its full range is exactly the fixed space of C: Cg=g iff there exists u with ιu=g. There exists a bounded complex-linear positive operator Dc on L²(μ;ℂ), with for every g, Dc g=ιD(Rg)+iιD(Qg), for every real u, Dc(ιu)=ι(Du), and for every complex g, C(Dc g)=Dc(Cg). No root or inverse is asserted.",
      "lean_proof": "Construct the actual quotient maps; Identify the real subspace and its norm; Build a bounded complex-linear operator; Cancel the imaginary cross terms; Prove both compatibility identities",
      "astis_dependencies": [],
      "mathlib_dependencies": [
        "ContinuousLinearMap.compLpL",
        "ContinuousLinearMap.coeFn_compLpL",
        "Lp.ext",
        "L2.inner_def",
        "integral_complex_ofReal",
        "ContinuousLinearMap.isPositive_iff_complex",
        "algebraMap_smul"
      ]
    }
  ]
